@ 29.1.1.1.7 - Proto-Athabaskan to Deg Hit’an
# citation: Whimemsz, from Krauss, Michael and Victor Golla (1981), “Northern Athapaskan Languages”. Handbook of North American Indians, Vol. 6 (Subarctic), 67 – 85
	{ TS, TŠ } > { TH, TS }
	TŠʷ > TṢ (
	TṢ ( > TS in [+ cons, - fr, + bk, + hi, - lo]uskokwim dialect)
	[+ cons, - fr, + bk, + hi, - lo] > [+ cons, - fr, + bk, + hi, - lo], TŠ
	w > v (
	v ( > w in Shageluk dialect)
	ɲ > ŋ
	{ R, F } > { R:[-voice], F:[-voice] } / _# in suffixes
